    pass 3 phase 2: one SQL implementation over the root — deals_landed_v1 + new_deals_batch_rows, the new_deals_batch procedure, lane C lands and CALLs
    
    The batch arithmetic lived in four places (main.py, the weekly script, the n8n Code node, the .mjs), held equal by tests. It is now
    one implementation over the raw root, with the pure part separable from the write part (docs/PASS3_RAW_ROOT.md §3, decisions D2–D5).
    
    - sql/deals_landed_v1.sql: S2 the VIEW deals_landed_v1 — one typed column per landed property (JSON_VALUE + SAFE_CAST, the HubSpot
      property names for both sources), name_key computed once; S7 the TABLE FUNCTION new_deals_batch_rows(run_ts, entity, orchestrator,
      window_start) — the slice's in-scope window, labels from labels_raw (id fallback), lane C's duplicate rule over every deal the root
      knows as of run_ts (latest observation per deal_id, 90-day horizon), hot_score_v1 with run_ts as "now"; column order = new_deals.
      Both read deals_raw / labels_raw only (no grant on the sync dataset needed).
    - sql/new_deals_batch.sql: S8 the PROCEDURE new_deals_batch(run_ts, entity, orchestrator, mode, advance_state, state_report_id,
      watermark_in, query_start, query_end, started_ms, gaps) — validation and the lane-A lease check first; labels_missing /
      dedup_horizon_partial decided here; TEMP batch from the table function; mode dry → one runs row (dry_run TRUE, rows_written 0),
      nothing else; otherwise ONE transaction: MERGE new_deals (frozen four untouched; an older slice never overwrites a newer
      observation) → history slice (an event deletes only its own deal) → runs row → report_state when advance_state (GREATEST, never
      rewinds); any error → ROLLBACK if open, FAILED runs row with the message, RAISE.
    - sql/new_deals_weekly.sql: DECLAREs → freshness guard → gaps → landing inside BEGIN … EXCEPTION (raw_landing_failed) →
      SET v_watermark_in → CALL new_deals_batch(…, TRUE, 'NEW_DEALS_<entity>_C', …, v_gaps). No transaction in the script.
    - sql/apply.sh applies the two new files last.
    - tests/test_pass3_sql.py (8 tests): the view types exactly main.PROPS; table-function columns == new_deals in order; the MERGE
      update list excludes the frozen four and covers every other column; no sync view is read; the procedure's contract; every
      emitted data_gaps value is in the vocabulary and each lane's values are emitted; apply order and placeholders;
      tests/pass3_batch_vectors.sql current — the EXECUTED check (dev dataset, credentials): the 15 vectors landed as a deals_raw slice,
      read through the view and the table function, score and flag compared, slice dropped.
    - docs: PASS3_RAW_ROOT.md "Phase 2 as implemented" (+ the fourth table-function parameter and the eleventh procedure parameter),
      lane-C cells L4–L8/L13 and one equality check in execution_surfaces.yaml (workbook rebuilt), architecture nodes + tree, README,
      timeline, recipe c_raw_batch.md.
    
    Behaviour change: lane C computes through the procedure (same rows: same name_key, same rule, same UDF, same frozen set, same
    report_id); lane A is untouched until phase 3. Rollback: re-register the previous script.
    
